  "mechanismSummary": "The first Mannich product enolises again (H₃O⁺ protonates the ketone, water removes a proton from the free CH₂), and its ring OH is protonated and pushed out by the nitrogen lone pair to make a second iminium ion. The enol carbon then attacks the iminium carbon inside the same molecule, closing a six-membered ring: an intramolecular Mannich reaction. Deprotonation gives tropinone-2,4-dicarboxylic acid, the 8-azabicyclo[3.2.1]octane (tropane) skeleton. The new ring can only close with the nitrogen bridge cis, which is why tropinone forms as a single, symmetrical (meso) bicycle; stereochemistry is explained here but not checked by the app yet. The CO₂H groups are drawn un-ionised for clarity.",
